Calculate the perimeter of this triangle. Give your answer in millimetres.

examples.solution_text:
Change the centimetre length to millimetres first.
$5.8\text{ cm}=58\text{ mm}$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.66,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(5.8,0) node[midway,below=5pt] {$58\text{ mm}$};
\draw[black] (5.8,0)--(4.41724138,4.49199049) node[midway,above right=5pt] {$47\text{ mm}$};
\draw[black] (4.41724138,4.49199049)--(0,0) node[midway,above left=5pt] {$63\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

All three lengths are now in millimetres.
$\begin{align*}P&=58+47+63\\&=168\text{ mm}\end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
Matching dashes show equal side lengths. Calculate the perimeter of this parallelogram in millimetres.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(4.2,0)--(5.4,1.6)--(1.2,1.6)--cycle;
\draw[black] (2.04,-0.1)--(2.04,0.1) (2.16,-0.1)--(2.16,0.1);
\draw[black] (3.24,1.5)--(3.24,1.7) (3.36,1.5)--(3.36,1.7);
\draw[black] (0.52,0.86)--(0.68,0.74) (4.72,0.86)--(4.88,0.74);
\path (3.3,1.6) node[above=6pt] {$42\text{ mm}$};
\path (0.6,0.8) node[left=6pt] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Convert the centimetres to millimetres.
$2\text{ cm}=20\text{ mm}$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(4.2,0)--(5.4,1.6)--(1.2,1.6)--cycle;
\draw[black] (2.04,-0.1)--(2.04,0.1) (2.16,-0.1)--(2.16,0.1);
\draw[black] (3.24,1.5)--(3.24,1.7) (3.36,1.5)--(3.36,1.7);
\draw[black] (0.52,0.86)--(0.68,0.74) (4.72,0.86)--(4.88,0.74);
\path (3.3,1.6) node[above=6pt] {$42\text{ mm}$};
\path (2.1,0) node[below=6pt] {$42\text{ mm}$};
\path (0.6,0.8) node[left=6pt] {$20\text{ mm}$};
\path (4.8,0.8) node[right=6pt] {$20\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The dashes show two sides of each length.
$\begin{align*}P&=2\times42+2\times20\\&=84+40\\&=124\text{ mm}\end{align*}$
